Exercise Drizzle’s public `db.transaction(...)` API on local and live Durable Objects, using the upstream fix in https://github.com/drizzle-team/drizzle-orm/pull/6325.

```ts
yield* db.transaction(Effect.fn(function* (tx) {
  yield* tx.insert(users).values({ name: "before" });
  yield* Effect.sleep("10 millis");
  yield* tx.insert(users).values({ name: "after" });
}));
```

The existing adapter can report rollback and then resume the callback outside the transaction. The upstream change delegates to Effect’s storage-backed transaction implementation, preserving suspension, nested rollback, cancellation, and caller context.

- Add public transaction coverage alongside the existing migration and SQL-client checks.
- Upgrade Effect to rc.116 for native nested transactions, with type-only adaptations for its stricter signatures.
- Include a reproducible workspace patch for the upstream Drizzle change. This patch applies only to this workspace; it does not fix consumers’ independent Drizzle installations.

