## Why
The first production test showed that one-pass extraction was not advisor-grade:
- ordinary Rina fallback model could be used for historical truth reconstruction;
- PDF text was flattened, losing document structure;
- one model pass had to both understand the job and fill database fields;
- repeated uploads could produce inconsistent interpretations;
- planned work/outcomes and financial completion could be overstated.

## New pipeline
- dedicated historical-document analyzer, separate from ordinary Rina chat;
- default model: `gpt-5.6-sol`, reasoning effort `high` (environment-overridable);
- original PDF is sent directly to the model, while page-preserving pypdf text is supplied as a searchable aid;
- Pass 1: whole-document Ajebo Fix advisor understanding and chronology;
- Pass 2: structured Aura candidates generated only from Pass-1 understanding;
- strict JSON-schema structured outputs;
- page/excerpt provenance and deterministic source-match checks;
- deterministic metadata fallback for Job/SOW references;
- financial facts forced to `observed → financial_separate`;
- durable Treatment Outcomes require `outcome_observed` plus a meaningful direction;
- identical PDFs reuse the same advisor-grade analysis;
- stored documents can be re-analyzed in place without uploading again;
- recent historical documents appear on the vehicle page for resume-after-login.

## Authority
No model output autonomously changes vehicle truth. Advisor review remains mandatory, and completed work still requires explicit advisor confirmation before application.

No Wave 3 / predictive-readiness changes.

