## Scope

Persists V1A temporal recurrence hypotheses into the existing Personal Context storage without turning inference into fact or authority.

V1B reuses MemoryClaimRow:
- predicate = context.pattern.temporal_recurrence
- source_quality = DERIVED_PATTERN
- status = ACTIVE
- staleness_class = PERISHABLE
- object_type = JSON

No new table and no migration.

## Admission

A hypothesis is accepted only when it remains:
- TEMPORAL_RECURRENCE;
- INFERRED;
- HYPOTHESIS;
- confidence >= 0.75;
- support_ratio >= 0.60;
- occurrence_count >= 3;
- non-expired;
- grants_authority = false;
- recommendation_ready = false.

Every referenced TimelineEvent must match tenant, actor, event type, signature and provenance and must not be SECRET.

## Idempotency / history

- exact same snapshot -> idempotent, same active claim;
- reinforced/changed snapshot -> previous claim becomes SUPERSEDED;
- new active claim points to previous via supersedes_claim_id;
- historical evidence remains preserved.

## Personal Context

The active hypothesis is visible through the existing bounded Personal Context snapshot.

Superseded snapshots remain stored but are excluded from active context.

## Safety boundary

V1B does not:
- create FactRow;
- create recommendation;
- request capability;
- execute action;
- grant disclosure authority;
- grant execution authority.

## Tests

- valid V1A hypothesis persists as governed MemoryClaim;
- no FactRow created;
- exact replay idempotent;
- reinforcement supersedes and preserves history;
- low confidence/support/expired rejected;
- authority/recommendation flags rejected;
- forged provenance rejected;
- cross-person evidence rejected.

