Physical two-device testing exposed an authority-expiry boundary during the Shared Transfer Challenge.

Observed production behavior:
- both devices showed FRESH PRIVATE SESSION REQUIRED;
- Daniel had a newly started live 14:51 transfer countdown and REQUEST EARLY END;
- Nik remained at 15:00 / waiting for coordinator;
- both surfaced JOURNEY_RECONNECT_PROGRESSION_NOT_AUTHORITATIVE.

Root cause:
- exact private sessions defaulted to 15 minutes, the same length as the transfer window;
- the session lifetime starts before setup/Career Start, so it can expire seconds after Transfer Challenge begins;
- an expired page-memory active session also blocked creating a fresh session;
- reconnect could race the expiry boundary and surface a secondary generic progression error.

This PR:
- extends the default private-session TTL to the already-supported 30-minute maximum;
- makes clock-expired page-memory sessions non-blocking for fresh host/join;
- marks expired held capabilities EXPIRED and disables stale copy/close/revoke actions;
- downgrades a reconnect expiry race into intended FRESH_SESSION_REQUIRED recovery;
- promotes the whole shell to r36 with r35 rollback.

