## Goal
Connect the finished game client to the versioned score server without making networking part of the run-completion critical path.

## Client contract
- submits Ruleset V2 / Campaign V2 payload;
- includes difficulty, completion stage, run seed, control mode, boss count, Bloodstream boss time, host-cell count, kills, highest level and total time;
- MAX and Telegram submit signed PlatformBridge.initData;
- messenger results without signed initData are not silently downgraded;
- browser uses a persistent anonymous id and remains server-side unverified/unranked;
- local dateKey is included for day-scoped server views.

## Routing / resilience
- uses relative `api/score`, preserving the production `/ofeliya/` namespace through Caddy -> nginx -> score-service;
- 2.5s abort timeout;
- failures return null and never block result UI, restart, menu or share actions.

## Result UI
- verified ranked response shows Ruleset/rank;
- unranked messenger result shows saved/out-of-ranking;
- browser shows test-result/out-of-ranking;
- network failure hides the status rather than disrupting the player.

## QA
Dedicated MAX browser smoke intercepts the real score request, verifies signed initData and the full V2 payload, returns rank #7, and asserts the result screen keeps retry/share/menu controls functional.

