Companion to [alfred-prime#26](https://github.com/DanielGGordon/alfred-prime/pull/26), which makes the Alfred Android app its own update channel. `android.md`'s meta-rule says a project that changes how it deploys Android updates this file in the same breath, so: the Alfred branch now documents the in-app update path.

What is recorded:

- `publish-apk.sh` writes `downloads/latest.json` next to the APK — no new service, no new route, still a file copy with no sudo;
- the manifest shape, and why `apk` is the *versioned* file name rather than `alfred-latest.apk`;
- the three places the phone checks (15-minute beat, `onResume` throttled to 10 minutes, the Settings button), the strictly-greater-`versionCode` rule and the sanity checks on the manifest;
- one notification per `versionCode`, the SHA-256 verify before the installer sees the file, the `FileProvider` `content://` hand-off, and the one-time `REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES` grant;
- what porting it to another project would take (the manifest step plus three files), and the one project it must **not** be given: anything release-signed by a key that might rotate.

The manual-checklist entry for the OEM installer now also covers the in-app update end to end, which is the part no emulator can stand in for.

Nothing else in the repo changes — no hooks, no skills, no settings — so `install.sh` only needs re-running for the symlink to pick up the new content after merge.

